wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(12530043512799715)
,p_plug_name=>'About Olist Copilot'
,p_title=>'About Olist Copilot'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>4072358936313175081
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_location=>null
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Olist Copilot is a demo application built on a real, anonymized e-commerce dataset (Olist, a Brazilian online marketplace) hosted entirely in an Oracle Autonomous Database on OCI. It started as a way to explore what a modern data + AI stack looks '
||'like end to end, and grew into this Oracle APEX front-end.</p>',
'',
'<h3>What it demonstrates</h3>',
'<ul>',
'<li><strong>Cloud database:</strong> every page here reads from the same live Oracle Autonomous Database (Always Free tier) &mdash; nothing runs locally.</li>',
'<li><strong>Text-to-SQL chat:</strong> the Chat page lets you ask a question in plain English. A FastAPI backend classifies the intent, has Claude generate the SQL, runs it against the database, and returns the results as a table and (when it fits) a'
||' chart.</li>',
'<li><strong>Machine learning:</strong> the Delivery Estimate page calls a trained regression model to predict how many days an order will take to arrive, based on the order and shipping details.</li>',
'<li><strong>Classic reporting:</strong> the Orders and Sellers pages are Interactive Reports/Grids over the same schema, for straightforward drill-down and search.</li>',
'</ul>',
'',
'<h3>The data</h3>',
'<p>The dataset covers roughly 100,000 real orders placed on the Olist marketplace between 2016 and 2018 &mdash; customers, products, sellers, payments, reviews, and delivery timestamps, all joined by order, product, seller, customer, and zip code key'
||'s. Here''s how the tables relate:</p>',
'<p><img src="#APP_FILES#olist_schema.png" alt="Olist database schema diagram" style="max-width:100%; height:auto; border:1px solid #ddd; padding:6px; margin:10px 0;"></p>',
'',
'<h3>Try it &mdash; example questions for Chat</h3>',
'<ul>',
'<li>How many orders were placed in total?</li>',
'<li>What are the top 10 product categories by revenue for year 2017?</li>',
'<li>Which sellers have the highest average review score?</li>',
'<li>What is the average delivery time by customer state?</li>',
'<li>How did monthly revenue change over 2017 and 2018?</li>',
'</ul>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
